{"case":{"approved_prefix":"django/","command":["python","/verification/verify.py"],"entry_files":["django/utils/dateparse.py"],"entry_lines":{"django/utils/dateparse.py":14},"id":"django__django-10999","image":"sha256:df8f0ef9be4fb1f710c20ba9738a4ec6fa68d2a1d6422fce277cbfc4b69ed73e","issue":"Fix parse_duration() for some negative durations\nDescription\n\t\nThe ​https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/2.1/_modules/django/utils/dateparse/ defines:\nstandard_duration_re = re.compile(\n\tr'^'\n\tr'(?:(?P<days>-?\\d+) (days?, )?)?'\n\tr'((?:(?P<hours>-?\\d+):)(?=\\d+:\\d+))?'\n\tr'(?:(?P<minutes>-?\\d+):)?'\n\tr'(?P<seconds>-?\\d+)'\n\tr'(?:\\.(?P<microseconds>\\d{1,6})\\d{0,6})?'\n\tr'$'\n)\nthat doesn't match to negative durations, because of the <hours> definition final (lookahead) part does not have '-?' in it. The following will work:\n\tr'((?:(?P<hours>-?\\d+):)(?=-?\\d+:-?\\d+))?'\n(Thanks to Konstantin Senichev for finding the fix.)\n","issue_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/10999","provenance":"Build004 curated SWE-bench Verified case; human-localized entry files. Public training contamination possible. Entry files and line windows derive from historical maintainer localization; reference text is not supplied to the model.","qualified":true,"reference_digest":"5f79fbb7e321b24ac8090df846218a64ff35048433bc1c818f1cbfd72ad58aab","repository":"django/django","revision":"36300ef336e3f130a0dadc1143163ff3d23dc843","source_digest":"cc1cdbff054033fc08c0ca5f8445dfe93d56e26e79dbb3232b39716e5e95394b","source_url":"https://github.com/django/django/tree/36300ef336e3f130a0dadc1143163ff3d23dc843","split":"evaluation","title":"Fix parse_duration() for some negative durations","verification_digest":"8597d6803fd3e0b7cbd649216f55179449632cdd4cf687f74be1e4c8119bc577"},"registry_version":"repository-cases-v1"}